{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 3, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a biographical drama film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the film is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich.\n\nthe film opens with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard university, as he is dumped by his girlfriend erica albright (played by rooney mara). this event sets off a chain of events that leads mark to create a website called \"facemash\", which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success, but also attracts the attention of the university's administration, who shut it down.\n\nmark is approached by cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who are members of the university's rowing team, with an idea for a social networking site called \"harvard connect\". mark agrees to work with them, but soon becomes obsessed with the idea and begins to work on his own version of the site, which he calls \"thefacebook\".\n\nthe film follows mark's journey as he creates the site, teams up with his friend eduardo saverin (played by andrew garfield), and becomes embroiled in a series of lawsuits with the winklevoss twins and eduardo. along the way, mark's relationships with his friends and family begin to deteriorate, and he becomes increasingly isolated and obsessed with his creation.\n\nthe film is shot in a dark and moody style, with a lot of use of shadows and muted colors. the score is also noteworthy, with a haunting and atmospheric soundtrack that adds to the overall mood of the film.\n\nthe performances in the film are also excellent, with jesse eisenberg delivering a standout performance as mark zuckerberg. he brings a level of depth and nuance to the character that is both captivating and unsettling. andrew garfield is also excellent as eduardo saverin, bringing a level of vulnerability and emotion to the character that makes him relatable and sympathetic.\n\nthe film's script is also noteworthy, with a lot of quick-witted and clever dialogue that adds to the overall sense of tension and drama. aaron sorkin's writing is both intelligent and engaging, and he does an excellent job of bringing the story to life.\n\noverall, the social network is a thought-provoking and engaging film that explores the darker side of ambition and success. it is a must-see for anyone interested in the story of facebook and the people behind it, and it is a testament to the power of film to tell complex and compelling stories.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.11627468466758728}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -1.6927862816373818e-05}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.03940759226679802}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.6689440599293448e-05}, {"token": " bi", "logprob": -2.392461061477661}, {"token": "ographical", "logprob": -1.1920930376163597e-07}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -5.245222382654902e-06}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.0008272373233921826}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -1.2764348983764648}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.007096676621586084}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -1.6689314179529902e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -8.344653679159819e-07}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.03567316010594368}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.0034006177447736263}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0005529859336093068}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.0014333262806758285}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.03310709819197655}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0019341923762112856}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.06060308590531349}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.10225341469049454}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.00314323860220611